# Slow Productivity — Cal Newport

Cal Newport's *Slow Productivity* challenges the cult of busyness, arguing for doing fewer things better. Key ideas include protecting unstructured time, choosing depth over breadth, and measuring productivity by value delivered rather than hours logged. Connects to the broader strategies mental model through its emphasis on strategic commitment and selective focus.
